British Citizen Act
===================


§ 1  Assumptions

The following are taken as given:

1. Person.

2. Mother of.

3. Father of.

4. Is born in the United Kingdom after commencement.

5. Is born in a qualifying territory after the appointed day.

6. Is settled in the United Kingdom.

7. Is settled in the qualifying territory in which the person is born.


§ 2  Improved Readability Version

Definitions:

1. Place consists of:
    - English name — text

2. Date consists of:
    - year — number
    - month — number
    - day — number

3. Maybe means one of Nothing or Just.

4. Natural Person consists of:
    - mama — Maybe of Person
    - papa — Maybe of Person
    - birthPlace — Maybe of Place
    - birthDate — Maybe of Date

Provisions:

1. Is BOT if:
    (a) the place's English name is Anguilla;
    (b) the place's English name is Bermuda;
    (c) the place's English name is British Antarctic Territory;
    (d) the place's English name is British Indian Ocean Territory;
    (e) the place's English name is Cayman Islands;
    (f) the place's English name is Falkland Islands;
    (g) the place's English name is Gibraltar;
    (h) the place's English name is Hong Kong;
    (i) the place's English name is Montserrat;
    (j) the place's English name is Pitcairn, Henderson, Ducie and Oeno Islands;
    (k) the place's English name is St Helena, Ascension and Tristan da Cunha;
    (l) the place's English name is Sovereign Base Areas of Akrotiri and Dhekelia;
    (m) the place's English name is South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands;
    (n) the place's English name is Turks and Caicos Islands; or
    (o) the place's English name is Virgin Islands.

2. Commencement is a Date with:
    - year — 1983
    - month — 1
    - day — 1

3. Appointed day is a Date with:
    - year — 2002
    - month — 2
    - day — 21

4. Qualifying territory if:
    (a) is BOT for the place; and
    (b) the place's English name is not Sovereign Base Areas of Akrotiri and Dhekelia.

5. After the date d and the date c if (year with the date c − 1900) × 365 + month with the date c × 30 + day with the date c is less than (the date d's year − 1900) × 365 + the date d's month × 30 + the date d's day.

6. Is born in UK if UK is English name with the natural person's birth place's val.

7. Is born in US if US is English name with p's birth place's val.

8. After commencement means after p's birth date's val and commencement.

9. After appointed day means after p's birth date's val and appointed day.

10. Plus equals a + b.


§ 3  Expanded version

1. Is a British citizen if anything if:
    (a) any of the following:
        (i) is born in the United Kingdom after commencement with the person; or
        (ii) is born in a qualifying territory after the appointed day with the person; and
    (b) any of the following:
        (i) is a British citizen if anything for father of the person and a;
        (ii) is a British citizen if anything for mother of the person and a;
        (iii) is settled in the United Kingdom with father of the person;
        (iv) is settled in the United Kingdom with mother of the person;
        (v) is settled in the qualifying territory in which the person is born with father of the person; or
        (vi) is settled in the qualifying territory in which the person is born with mother of the person.


§ 4  Version using a local auxiliary declaration

1. Is a British citizen (local) if:
    (a) any of the following:
        (i) is born in the United Kingdom after commencement with the person; or
        (ii) is born in a qualifying territory after the appointed day with the person; and
    (b) any of the following:
        (i) father or mother with is settled in the United Kingdom; or
        (ii) father or mother with is settled in the qualifying territory in which the person is born.
    where:
    - Father or mother if:
        (a) property with father of the person; or
        (b) property with mother of the person.


§ 5  Version using a global auxiliary declaration

1. For father or mother of [person] and [property] if:
    (a) property with father of person; or
    (b) property with mother of person.

2. Is a British citizen (variant) if:
    (a) any of the following:
        (i) is born in the United Kingdom after commencement with the person; or
        (ii) is born in a qualifying territory after the appointed day with the person; and
    (b) any of the following:
        (i) for father or mother of the person and is a British citizen (variant);
        (ii) for father or mother of the person and is settled in the United Kingdom; or
        (iii) for father or mother of the person and is settled in the qualifying territory in which the person is born.


§ 6  Schedule 1: British Overseas Territories

1. British Overseas Territories means the following list of Place:
    | English name                                      |
    |---------------------------------------------------|
    | Anguilla                                          |
    | Bermuda                                           |
    | British Antarctic Territory                       |
    | British Indian Ocean Territory                    |
    | Cayman Islands                                    |
    | Falkland Islands                                  |
    | Gibraltar                                         |
    | Hong Kong                                         |
    | Montserrat                                        |
    | Pitcairn, Henderson, Ducie and Oeno Islands       |
    | St Helena, Ascension and Tristan da Cunha         |
    | South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands      |
    | The Sovereign Base Areas of Akrotiri and Dhekelia |
    | Turks and Caicos Islands                          |
    | Virgin Islands                                    |


